---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import SiteMenu from '../components/SiteMenu.astro';
import { SITE_NAME, SITE_TITLE, pageHref } from '../lib/site';
---
<Base title={`About · ${SITE_NAME}`}>
  <header class="wrap site-head">
    <a class="site-name" href={pageHref()}>{SITE_NAME}</a>
    <div class="head-end">
      <nav class="site-nav" aria-label="Back">
        <a href={pageHref()}>All movements</a>
      </nav>
      <SiteMenu current="about" />
    </div>
  </header>
  <main id="main" class="wrap">
    <article class="prose">
      <h1>About</h1>
      <p>Since ChatGPT arrived in November 2022, it has felt as if history started again with AI. It didn't. The people building AI, and those resisting it, carry ideas with long histories, and those ideas have names: transhumanism, techno-optimism, AI safety and others.</p>
      <p>{SITE_NAME} is an investigation of those ideas, mapped as twelve movements in six families. It starts with what each one holds today and follows its roots back in time. Anyone can then see where the arguments about AI come from, and speak about them with a shared vocabulary.</p>
      <p>The movements range from those who expect AI to take us beyond human limits to those for whom it is a normal technology. Each answers two old questions in its own way: what should stay human, and who should decide? Alongside them run the history of AI, the people involved, the words they fight with, and themes still being researched.</p>
      <p>It is developed alongside a planned exhibition and keeps growing: new movements, words and roots are added as the research goes on.</p>
      <p class="mono" style="font-size: 14px; color: #555555">First draft. All texts are being checked against their sources.</p>
    </article>
  </main>
</Base>
